{"name":"Shortbread","hex":"#f5e6d3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shortbread","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of biscuit (cookie), popular in Britain, traditionally made from one part sugar, two parts butter and three parts flour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shortbread"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shortbread","blocks":[{"text":"Shortbread or shortie is a traditional Scottish biscuit usually made from one part white sugar, two parts butter and three to four parts plain wheat flour. Shortbread does not contain leavening, such as baking powder or baking soda. Shortbread is widely associated with Christmas and Hogmanay festivities in Scotland, and some Scottish brands are exported around the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Shortbread_House_round_biscuit_.jpg/330px-Shortbread_House_round_biscuit_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shortbread","wikidata":"Q652695"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Malcolms_Scottish_shortbread_%287519979640%29.jpg/500px-Malcolms_Scottish_shortbread_%287519979640%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Malcolms_Scottish_shortbread_%287519979640%29.jpg/1280px-Malcolms_Scottish_shortbread_%287519979640%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Malcolms_Scottish_shortbread_%287519979640%29.jpg/500px-Malcolms_Scottish_shortbread_%287519979640%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shortbread fingers and petticoat tails","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMalcolms_Scottish_shortbread_(7519979640).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/